- The key exists, persists, and is readable without the strip being mounted.
- A test asserts that disabling produces a state in which no companion session may run —
  written so it still passes before Epic D exists, and becomes meaningful once it does.
- Labels are catalog strings (D-21/D-102), not literals; coordinate the namespace with C5.', 'in_progress', 'high', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-09 03:00:37.055', '2026-08-09 10:34:06.140', NULL, '1b1de6d2bc4a72d2421aa0b0497da43a', 2) ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_record_id=excluded.parent_record_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at >= tickets.updated_at;
